          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Beulah"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good, basic, easy crab quiche recipe. Added a third egg. Substituted 1 cup low-fat, small curd cottage cheese for milk and 1/4 cup of the mayo (I beat the living daylights out of the first mixture to make sure there would be no curds in the final product). Used 2 six-ounce cans of crab meat. Added a small jar of pimentos for more color. Seasoned with Tony Chachere's Creole seasoning (which would make dirt taste great). If you're an experienced cook, you can change and add to this recipe a lot. I just use what needs to be used out of my fridge.",
            "datePublished": "2019-07-07T14:42:33.050Z"
          }
